#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Say where the published benchmark reports stand against main; publish a finished pass.

Extensionless and executable because agents type it as a command mid-session,
like survey-due, stalled-prs and state.

bench-report.yml regenerates the five published benchmark files on a runner
and hands them back as an artifact (#1324); a seat downloads it and pushes
the files on its own token. The ratio gate pins compress() bytes and no
longer demands the reports in a codec PR (ADR-0076, #1437): the pass on main
after the merge is the one writer. A change to the report binaries themselves
(#1356, #1367, #1373 and #1376 added the competitor frontier to both reports)
lands on main the same way, and the committed reports stay as they were
until a publish PR, with nothing else to say so. Two maintainer runs on 2026-10-19
named the dispatch a blocker for want of a token the seat holds
(agent-heartbeat.yml grants `actions: write` for exactly this). A duty two
wakes apart, dispatch then download, held in a model's memory across runs,
is the shape ADR-0022 says to compile.

Three facts decide, every one read from main through gh, so the answer does
not depend on the caller's checkout or branch:

    affecting   the newest commit on main under the push paths
                bench-report.yml lists on main, read from that file so the
                trigger and this detector cannot disagree: the inputs whose
                change moves what the reports print. `src/` is not among
                them, `bench/baseline.json` is: the gate's digest pin
                (#1254) makes every PR whose compress() output moves on
                the gate cases commit a regenerated baseline, so that file's
                merge is the codec's signal, about one a day against ten
                src/ commits. `check` does not read the reports (ADR-0076),
                so the list is the only demand: the list was `bench/src`
                alone, and #1423 moved six Silesia finals and no bpb
                (every digest, by the version byte), so the finals sat
                stale behind a `fresh` read. What still
                escapes: a change that leaves every digest intact while
                moving inputs the gate cases do not resemble (the one
                long case, #1434, holds a single repeat past the standard
                reach), and one that moves speed alone. One list to widen, with
                the cost in mind: every pass is serial by design (#1321)
                and every regenerated report differs in its timing
                columns, so a wider list is more publish PRs of runner
                jitter.
    generated   the commit on main the committed reports were generated at.
                A publish commit names it in its subject, the title this
                script prints for the publish PR ("regenerated at <sha>").
                A reports commit that names none is stale by rule, never
                fresh: the publish PR is the reports' one writer
                (ADR-0076), so such a commit is a hand edit, and the next
                publish overwrites it with a pass's output. Not UNREADABLE,
                because `--publish` needs state publish and a revert names
                no generator either, so that answer would deadlock on the
                one commit nothing honest writes (#1381). The reports
                commit's own date would not do: a publish PR for pass P
                can merge after a later report-affecting commit B lands,
                and then the reports are newer than B by date while B's
                pass is unpublished (the reviewer's sequence on #1378).
    pass        the newest bench-report.yml run on main. It covers the
                affecting commit when its head is at or after it; main is
                linear (squash merges), so committer dates order it, and a
                newer run's head is never older than an older run's, so only
                the newest run can cover.

States, the first word of the first line, in the order tested:

    fresh           generated is at or after affecting; nothing owed. Never
                    this when the reports commit names no generator.
    running <id>    the newest pass covers and is in progress; nothing to
                    do this wake, the next one publishes.
    publish <id>    the newest pass covers, succeeded, and its artifact is
                    live: `bench-report --publish` writes the five files
                    into the tree, `cargo x check` then names the README
                    and site quotes the new timing columns moved
                    (tests/claims.rs pins them, so a PR of the five files
                    alone fails `test`, #1384), and push-branch and gh-pr
                    ship all of it under the title this prints, which is
                    where the next read learns the generator.
    dispatch        generated predates affecting and no live pass covers it
                    (none, failed, cancelled, or its artifact expired):
                    one `gh workflow run` on GH_WORKFLOW_TOKEN.
    UNREADABLE      gh could not answer; the reason follows. Never an empty
                    result, because a false `fresh` is the silent stale
                    report this exists to end.

bench-report.yml runs on every push to main under those paths, so `dispatch`
is the healing state for a pass that was cancelled, failed or expired
unpublished, not the routine one.

Liveness: the footer always names the three facts it read, so a reader can
tell fresh reports from a detector that stopped reading.

Usage: bench-report              print the state and the next action
       bench-report --publish    in state publish: download the artifact and
                                 write its files into the tree

Exits 0 whichever state it prints; a state is a duty, not an error.
`--publish` exits 1 when the state is not publish or the download fails.
"""

import argparse
import base64
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

import yaml

WORKFLOW = "bench-report.yml"
ARTIFACT = "bench-report"
REPORTS = ("docs/benchmarks/canterbury.md", "docs/benchmarks/silesia.md")
# What the pass uploads, in bench-report.yml's `path:` order.
FILES = (
    "bench/baseline.json",
    "docs/benchmarks/baseline.md",
    "docs/benchmarks/baseline.svg",
    "docs/benchmarks/canterbury.md",
    "docs/benchmarks/silesia.md",
)
DISPATCH = f'GH_TOKEN="$GH_WORKFLOW_TOKEN" gh workflow run {WORKFLOW} --ref main'
# The publish PR's title, and so the squash commit's subject: the one place
# the generator is recorded, and GENERATOR is how the next read finds it.
TITLE = "bench: publish the reports regenerated at {sha}"
FULL_SHA = 40
# Twelve characters, because seven resolved once as no object (the docstring
# of `commit`); the regex admits seven for the five publish subjects on main
# that carry them.
SHORT_SHA = 12
GENERATOR = re.compile(rf"regenerated at ([0-9a-f]{{7,{FULL_SHA}}})\b")


def gh(*args):
    """Run gh; return (parsed JSON, None) or (None, reason). Never dies.

    Dying would answer no state, and a caller with no answer reads the
    reports' freshness by eye, which is the failure this replaces.
    """
    proc = subprocess.run(["gh", *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        lines = proc.stderr.strip().splitlines()
        return None, (lines[-1] if lines else f"gh exited {proc.returncode}")
    try:
        return json.loads(proc.stdout), None
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return None, "response was not JSON"


def report_paths(repo):
    """The workflow's `on.push.paths` on main, as commit-API path prefixes (a trailing `/**` dropped).

    PyYAML reads the bare key `on` as the boolean True, so both spellings
    are tried.
    """
    row, error = gh("api", f"repos/{repo}/contents/.github/workflows/{WORKFLOW}?ref=main")
    if error:
        return None, f"{WORKFLOW} on main: {error}"
    try:
        doc = yaml.safe_load(base64.b64decode(row["content"]).decode())
    except (KeyError, ValueError, yaml.YAMLError) as exc:
        return None, f"{WORKFLOW} on main: {exc}"
    triggers = doc.get("on") or doc.get(True) or {}
    paths = (triggers.get("push") or {}).get("paths") or []
    if not paths:
        return None, f"{WORKFLOW} on main lists no push paths"
    return tuple(p[: -len("/**")] if p.endswith("/**") else p for p in paths), None


def commit(repo, sha):
    """A commit on the repository as {"sha", "date"}, by full sha, prefix or ref.

    `commits/{sha}` resolves a prefix against every object in the repository
    network, forks and dead PR heads included, and seven hex characters are
    not always one object there: `e4e3444`, named by 7162ea1 ("bench:
    publish the reports regenerated at e4e3444"), answered 422 "No commit
    found" while its eighth character resolved and every earlier publish
    prefix did (#1495). A prefix the endpoint refuses is asked of commit
    search, which indexes commits alone: one hit names the full sha, read
    back through the endpoint so every date has one shape (search stamps
    milliseconds, the endpoint does not, and `fresh` compares the strings);
    any other count stays unreadable naming both answers. A full sha is
    never retried, because nothing else can know it.
    """
    row, error = gh("api", f"repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}")
    if error and len(sha) < FULL_SHA:
        found, reason = gh("api", f"search/commits?q=repo:{repo}+hash:{sha}")
        hits = found.get("items", []) if isinstance(found, dict) else []
        if len(hits) == 1:
            return commit(repo, hits[0]["sha"])
        return None, f"{error}; commit search: {reason or f'{len(hits)} commits'}"
    if error:
        return None, error
    return {"sha": row["sha"], "date": row["commit"]["committer"]["date"]}, None


def newest_commit(repo, paths):
    """The newest commit on main touching any of `paths`, as {"sha", "date", "path", "subject"}."""
    best = None
    for path in paths:
        rows, error = gh("api", f"repos/{repo}/commits?sha=main&path={path}&per_page=1")
        if error:
            return None, f"commits under {path}: {error}"
        if not rows:
            continue
        message = rows[0]["commit"].get("message") or ""
        row = {
            "sha": rows[0]["sha"],
            "date": rows[0]["commit"]["committer"]["date"],
            "path": path,
            "subject": message.splitlines()[0] if message else "",
        }
        if best is None or row["date"] > best["date"]:
            best = row
    if best is None:
        return None, f"no commit on main touches {', '.join(paths)}"
    return best, None


def generator(subject):
    """The pass head a publish commit names in its subject, or None when the commit is its own generator."""
    hit = GENERATOR.search(subject or "")
    return hit.group(1) if hit else None


def fresh(generated, affecting):
    """Whether the reports need nothing: generated at or after affecting, and generated at all."""
    return generated is not None and generated["date"] >= affecting["date"]


def read(repo):
    """The facts `decide` needs, read lazily: the pass's head and artifact only when the reports are stale."""
    paths, error = report_paths(repo)
    if error:
        return None, error
    affecting, error = newest_commit(repo, paths)
    if error:
        return None, error
    reports, error = newest_commit(repo, REPORTS)
    if error:
        return None, error
    named = generator(reports["subject"])
    if named is None:
        generated = None
    else:
        generated, error = commit(repo, named)
        if error:
            return None, f"generator {named}, named by {reports['sha'][:7]}: {error}"
    runs, error = gh(
        "run",
        "list",
        "--repo",
        repo,
        "--workflow",
        WORKFLOW,
        "--branch",
        "main",
        "--limit",
        "1",
        "--json",
        "databaseId,status,conclusion,headSha,createdAt,updatedAt,url",
    )
    if error:
        return None, f"runs of {WORKFLOW} on main: {error}"
    newest = runs[0] if runs else None
    head = live = None
    if newest is not None and not fresh(generated, affecting):
        row, error = commit(repo, newest["headSha"])
        if error:
            return None, f"head of run {newest['databaseId']}: {error}"
        head = row["date"]
        if head >= affecting["date"] and newest["status"] == "completed" and newest["conclusion"] == "success":
            data, error = gh("api", f"repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{newest['databaseId']}/artifacts")
            if error:
                return None, f"artifacts of run {newest['databaseId']}: {error}"
            live = any(a["name"] == ARTIFACT and not a["expired"] for a in data.get("artifacts", []))
    return {
        "affecting": affecting,
        "reports": reports,
        "generated": generated,
        "newest": newest,
        "head": head,
        "live": live,
    }, None


def decide(affecting, generated, newest, head, live):
    """The state and its reason. Pure: every input is a fact `read` produced.

    `generated` is the commit the reports were generated at, None when the
    reports commit names no generator (stale by rule), `newest` the newest
    pass on main or None, `head` its head commit's date (None when not
    read), `live` whether its artifact is still downloadable (None when
    not read).
    """
    if fresh(generated, affecting):
        return "fresh", None
    if newest is None or head is None or head < affecting["date"]:
        return "dispatch", "no pass on main at or after it"
    if newest["status"] != "completed":
        return "running", None
    if newest["conclusion"] != "success":
        return "dispatch", f"the newest pass, {newest['databaseId']}, concluded {newest['conclusion']}"
    if not live:
        return "dispatch", f"the newest pass, {newest['databaseId']}, succeeded but its artifact expired"
    return "publish", None


def render(facts, error, out=sys.stdout):
    """Print the state line, the next action, and the liveness footer. Returns the state word."""
    if error is not None:
        print(f"bench-report: UNREADABLE ({error})", file=out)
        print("    Re-run once. A pass this cannot see is not a pass that ran, and reports", file=out)
        print("    this cannot date are not fresh.", file=out)
        return "UNREADABLE"

    affecting, reports, generated, newest = (facts[k] for k in ("affecting", "reports", "generated", "newest"))
    state, reason = decide(affecting, generated, facts["newest"], facts["head"], facts["live"])
    origin = (
        f"generated at {generated['sha'][:7]} {generated['date']}"
        if generated is not None
        else "naming no generator, stale by rule"
    )
    where = f"the reports ({reports['sha'][:7]}, {origin})"
    stale = f"{where} predate {affecting['sha'][:7]} ({affecting['date']}, under {affecting['path']})"
    if state == "fresh":
        print(
            f"fresh: {where} are at or after the newest report-affecting commit"
            f" ({affecting['sha'][:7]}, {affecting['date']}).",
            file=out,
        )
    elif state == "running":
        print(f"running {newest['databaseId']}: a pass on main started {newest['createdAt']} covers it; {stale}.", file=out)
        print("    Nothing to do this wake. The wake after it finishes publishes.", file=out)
        print(f"    {newest['url']}", file=out)
    elif state == "publish":
        print(f"publish {newest['databaseId']}: a pass on main finished {newest['updatedAt']} covers it; {stale}.", file=out)
        print("    Next: .github/scripts/bench-report --publish, which writes the five files into the tree;", file=out)
        print("    then `cargo x check`: tests/claims.rs pins README.md and site/index.html to the reports'", file=out)
        print("    date, CPU model and MB/s and names each quote the new reports moved, so fix those in", file=out)
        print("    the same diff (#1384); then push-branch and gh-pr ship it all, under this title and no", file=out)
        print("    other, because the next read learns the generator from it:", file=out)
        print(f'    "{TITLE.format(sha=newest["headSha"][:SHORT_SHA])}"', file=out)
        print(f"    {newest['url']}", file=out)
    else:
        print(f"dispatch: {stale}, and {reason}.", file=out)
        print(f"    Next: {DISPATCH}", file=out)
        print("    One command, not a unit of work; the pass runs on the runner and a later wake publishes.", file=out)

    print(
        f"\nbench-report: {state}"
        f" | affecting {affecting['sha'][:7]} {affecting['date']} under {affecting['path']}"
        f" | reports {reports['sha'][:7]} {origin}"
        f" | pass {newest['databaseId'] if newest else 'none'}"
        " | gh readable",
        file=out,
    )
    return state


def publish(repo, run_id, root, out=sys.stdout):
    """Download the pass's artifact and write FILES into the tree under `root`. Returns the exit code."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as scratch:
        proc = subprocess.run(
            ["gh", "run", "download", str(run_id), "--repo", repo, "-n", ARTIFACT, "-D", scratch],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
        )
        if proc.returncode != 0:
            lines = proc.stderr.strip().splitlines()
            print(f"bench-report: download of run {run_id} failed: {lines[-1] if lines else proc.returncode}", file=out)
            return 1
        for rel in FILES:
            if not (Path(scratch) / rel).is_file():
                print(f"bench-report: the artifact of run {run_id} lacks {rel}; nothing written", file=out)
                return 1
        for rel in FILES:
            shutil.copyfile(Path(scratch) / rel, root / rel)
    status = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(root), "status", "--short", "--", *FILES], capture_output=True, text=True)
    print(f"published run {run_id}: {len(FILES)} files written into the tree", file=out)
    print(status.stdout.rstrip() or "    identical to the tree: nothing to ship", file=out)
    return 0


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Where the published benchmark reports stand against main.")
    parser.add_argument("--publish", action="store_true", help="in state publish, write the pass's files into the tree")
    parser.add_argument("--repo", default=os.environ.get("GITHUB_REPOSITORY", "bugabinga/mothergod"), help="owner/name")
    args = parser.parse_args()

    facts, error = read(args.repo)
    state = render(facts, error)
    if not args.publish:
        return 0
    if state != "publish":
        print(f"\nbench-report: --publish needs state publish, not {state}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    root = Path(subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.strip())
    return publish(args.repo, facts["newest"]["databaseId"], root)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
